perl-cross: build the real DynaLoader (dl_none.xs) in a static perl

perl-cross builds no DynaLoader when usedl=undef. Upstream Configure
builds it with ext/DynaLoader/dl_none.xs: DynaLoader is present, and
every dynamic load croaks. With dlsrc=dl_none.xs (hints/wasix) the
Makefile now keeps dynaloader=DynaLoader, so DynaLoader.o goes into
libperl.a and writemain registers the real boot_DynaLoader in
perlmain.c. Replaces patches/0004 (the no-op boot_DynaLoader marker).
homescoop#186. Applied by build.sh (patch -p1 after the perl-cross
overlay).

--- a/Makefile.config.SH
+++ b/Makefile.config.SH
@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@
 	fi
 }
 
-if [ "$usedl" = 'undef' ]; then
+if [ "$usedl" = 'undef' -a "$dlsrc" != 'dl_none.xs' ]; then
 	dynaloader=''
 else
 	dynaloader="DynaLoader"
